// Browser Credential Store Accessed From the Command Line
// Detects a process other than the browser itself naming a browser's saved password or cookie store (Chromium Login Data, Cookies, Local State; Firefox key4.db, logins.json) on its command line. Infostealers and hands-on operators copy these files out before decrypting them offline.
// techniques: T1555.003   severity: high   status: experimental
// validate: Atomic Red Team T1555.003
//   copy "%LOCALAPPDATA%\Google\Chrome\User Data\Default\Login Data" %TEMP%\ld.db
// source: rules/credential-access/browser-credential-store-access.yml  (GENERATED, do not edit by hand)
Event
| where (((CommandLine contains @"\User Data\Default\Login Data" or CommandLine contains @"\User Data\Default\Network\Cookies" or CommandLine contains @"\User Data\Local State" or CommandLine contains @"\key4.db" or CommandLine contains @"\logins.json")) and not ((NewProcessName endswith @"\chrome.exe" or NewProcessName endswith @"\msedge.exe" or NewProcessName endswith @"\firefox.exe" or NewProcessName endswith @"\brave.exe" or NewProcessName endswith @"\opera.exe")))
